drm/msm: remove the D1/G1 diagnostics (DSIDBG); DPU core clock back to dynamic

Removed: D1 clock-status probe, DSI/INTF register dump, error-IRQ masking after 2000 errors, link
clock stall checks + logs, dsi_tpg test-pattern param, forced max DPU core clock, INTF timing print;
per-resume RGMU info prints downgraded to debug. Kept and relabelled (downstream parity used by the
working panel bring-up): DMA_FIFO_CTRL value, BLOCK_DMA_WITHIN_FRAME left clear, PHY_RESET bit 24,
video-mode enable split, HS TX timeout, TPG DMA mode clear, byte-clock rounding (upstream 6cd33b6f4155).
Verified #180: dsi_err 0, underruns 0, MDP clock 192 MHz dynamic, 40-round animation stress clean.

